  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, \r\rLocation Plan\rBlock Plan 002 Rev A\r010\r011\r012\r210\r211\r212\rPlanning, Design and Access Statement\rManufacturers specification Guide \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To preserve the visual character and architectural interest of the non-designated heritage asset.\r\r",
    "Prior to any above ground works, details of the proposed doors and windows shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall be a scale of 1:20 with 1:5 sections (including cills, reveals, heads, window furniture etc.). The proposed windows and doors shall be installed in accordance with the approved details and shall be permanently maintained as such. \r\rReason: to preserve the visual character and architectural interest of the non-designated heritage asset.\r"
